## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region sagas with per-tenant isolation, durable storage, and reliable cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across regions with CQRS and Event Sourcing
- Per-tenant event envelopes and outbox pattern
- Compensating actions and idempotent handlers
- Replay-safe projections and cross-region read-model updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch (pseudo)
function startSaga(tenantId, mediaId){
  const sagaId = uuid();
  persistSaga({id:sagaId, tenantId, mediaId, step:'Transcode', status:'in_progress'});
  publish({type:'Ingest', payload:{tenantId, mediaId, sagaId}});
}
function handleFailure(sagaId, failedStep){
  const comp = {Transcode:'DeleteTempArtifacts', PublishEU:'RevokePublishEU'}[failedStep];
  publish({type:'Compensate', payload:{sagaId, action:comp}});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency across services during retries?
- How would you observe and reconcile outbox vs. internal state across regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly, real-world saga with event-sourcing and CQRS: how to coordinate cross-service work, model event contracts, and ensure idempotent handlers with an outbox.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography in a write-side workflow
- Event contracts and read-model sketching for status tracking
- Outbox pattern and correlation-based deduplication

## Code Example
```javascript
// Map write events to commands (simplified)
function mapEventToCommand(evt){
  switch(evt.type){
    case 'ContentSubmitted':
      return { type: 'ModerationRequest', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId, correlationId: evt.id } }
    case 'ModerationApproved':
      return { type: 'PublishContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
    case 'ModerationRejected':
      return { type: 'HideContent', payload: { contentId: evt.contentId } }
  }
}

// Deduplication (idempotent handler)
if (outbox.has(correlationId)) return; outbox.add(correlationId);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotence guarantees and read-model integrity?
- What are trade-offs of in-process vs distributed saga orchestration for this flow?

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates your ability to design scalable, multi-tenant storage systems with zero-downtime operational capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- **Sharding Strategy**: Tenant_id-based consistent hashing with range partitions to ensure even distribution and minimize hotspots
- **Replication Topology**: Multi-region 3-way replication with leader-follower consensus for durability and availability
- **Online Rebalancing**: Versioned migration system with dual-write periods and gradual traffic shifting
- **Isolation & Security**: Per-tenant namespaces with dedicated access controls and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: migration plan snippet
async function migrateShard(oldShard, newShard) {
  await startTransfer(oldShard, newShard);
  await verifyIntegrity(oldShard, newShard);
  await switchTraffic(oldShard, newShard);
  await completeMigration(oldShard);
}
```
